  "finding": "Six of seven required workflows passed on the exact source SHA. Rust CI failed only the dependency-layer check on Ubuntu, macOS, and Windows; all workspace tests, formatting, and Clippy passed on those platforms, and the Rust 1.95 locked workspace tests passed. The pinned Obsidian 1.14.4 round-trip passed on all three platforms; the known-field Canvas source remained byte-identical with SHA-256 2258580368625a06b2b3d2f5b0576b032678b0a7bc73d1292716642c9c7f4cc5 after first shutdown and reopen. The Rust slice is not accepted until the intended engine-to-document dependency is added to the layer policy and all seven workflows pass on a fresh exact SHA.",
  "correction": "Allow openobsidian-engine to depend on openobsidian-doc in the xtask layer map. The engine is the application workflow boundary that composes pure Canvas parsing/editing with the vault revision check and journaled write. Keep doc independent and retain vault -> doc and engine -> vault boundaries.",
